# Executive Director (JF) > 2. Strategy and organizational direction
JF is responsible for:
defining OCE’s strategic priorities and positioning;

# Executive Director (JF) > 2. Strategy and organizational direction
JF is responsible for:
deciding which services, partnerships and organizational capabilities OCE should develop;

# Executive Director (JF) > 2. Strategy and organizational direction
JF is responsible for:
ensuring that OCE’s activities remain aligned with its mission;

# Executive Director (JF) > 2. Strategy and organizational direction
JF is responsible for:
evaluating opportunities against their impact, cost, complexity and risk;

# Executive Director (JF) > 2. Strategy and organizational direction
JF is responsible for:
translating strategic priorities into clear objectives for the team;

# Executive Director (JF) > 2. Strategy and organizational direction
JF is responsible for:
deciding what OCE will not pursue when capacity or risk does not justify it;

# Executive Director (JF) > 2. Strategy and organizational direction
JF is responsible for:
adapting the organizational structure as OCE’s activities evolve;

# Executive Director (JF) > 3. Governance and Board relationship
JF:
keeps the Board informed about OCE’s activities, financial position, principal risks and material commitments;

# Executive Director (JF) > 3. Governance and Board relationship
JF:
prepares the information and proposals required for Board decisions;

# Executive Director (JF) > 3. Governance and Board relationship
JF:
implements Board decisions and follows up on agreed actions;

# Executive Director (JF) > 3. Governance and Board relationship
JF:
ensures that governance requirements, delegations and decision records are clear;

# Executive Director (JF) > 3. Governance and Board relationship
JF:
escalates matters that exceed his delegated authority or require formal Board approval;

# Executive Director (JF) > 4. Financial governance and resource allocation
He:
sets financial priorities and planning assumptions;

# Executive Director (JF) > 4. Financial governance and resource allocation
He:
reviews budgets, forecasts, cash visibility and management information prepared with Michael;

# Executive Director (JF) > 4. Financial governance and resource allocation
He:
decides material spending priorities and resource trade-offs within his authority;

# Executive Director (JF) > 4. Financial governance and resource allocation
He:
